Without MPI, SuperCommunicator::communicate() only calls copy() and never
wait(). The HIP copy tasks run on non-blocking streams, so they neither wait
for earlier kernels on other streams nor finish before the caller continues.
The PostCollide population copy can then overlap stream()'s pointer rotation,
which makes periodic-overlap fields nondeterministic. Order and complete the
copies here.
--- a/src/core/platform/gpu/hip/communicator.hh
+++ b/src/core/platform/gpu/hip/communicator.hh
@@ -886,5 +886,9 @@ void ConcreteBlockCommunicator<ConcreteBlockLattice<T,DESCRIPTOR,Platform::GPU_HIP>>::copy()
 {
+  gpu::hip::device::synchronize();
   for (auto& task : _copyTasks) {
     task->copy();
   }
+  for (auto& task : _copyTasks) {
+    task->wait();
+  }
 }
